    {
      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.57,
      "end": 2.07,
      "text": "Hi, how are you holding up?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.99,
      "end": 15.35,
      "text": "Sadly, scattering seed on lawn rarely works. Grass is too competitive and smothers the seedlings."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.55,
      "end": 25.62,
      "text": "Strip off the turf in that patch, and don't add compost. Wildflowers actually like poor soil. Then sow in autumn or spring."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 30.91,
      "end": 37.31,
      "text": "Then you're halfway there. Another trick is a plant called yellow rattle. It weakens the grass so flowers can get in."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 41.02,
      "end": 47.58,
      "text": "Once a year in late summer, after the flowers set seed. Leave the cuttings a few days so the seeds drop, then rake them up."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 55.3,
      "end": 60.34,
      "text": "Start small, maybe a couple of metres square. You can always expand it once you see what comes up."
    }
  ]
